From 6cdf71da80873c7071c3edb3a5fae78feda35da8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: apocelipes <seve3r@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Mar 2026 04:14:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] win: fix const correctness compiler error (#5049)

libuv 1.52.1 changed uv_cpu_info_s.model from 'char*' to 'const char*'
in include/uv.h, but src/win/util.c was not updated. uv_cpu_info() takes
the address of that field and passes it to uv__convert_utf16_to_utf8(),
which is declared as taking 'char**', so the argument is now
'const char**' and no longer converts:

  src/win/util.c:630:31: error: passing argument 3 of
      'uv__convert_utf16_to_utf8' from incompatible pointer type
      [-Wincompatible-pointer-types]

GCC has treated -Wincompatible-pointer-types as an error by default
since GCC 14, so this breaks nativesdk-libuv for the mingw32 SDK. Only
the Windows backend is affected; the unix backends assign to the field
rather than taking its address.

The fix landed upstream five days after the 1.52.1 release and is not in
any tag yet - 1.52.1 is still the newest. Drop this patch once oe-core
carries the fix or ships a libuv newer than 1.52.1.

Upstream-Status: Backport [6cdf71da80873c7071c3edb3a5fae78feda35da8]
---
 src/win/util.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/win/util.c b/src/win/util.c
index fec07b269f7..bd9f7a67c13 100644
--- a/src/win/util.c
+++ b/src/win/util.c
@@ -627,7 +627,7 @@ int uv_cpu_info(uv_cpu_info_t** cpu_infos_ptr, int* cpu_count_ptr) {
 
     uv__convert_utf16_to_utf8(cpu_brand,
                               cpu_brand_size / sizeof(WCHAR),
-                              &(cpu_info->model));
+                              (char**) &(cpu_info->model));
   }
 
   uv__free(sppi);
